{
  "_doc": [
    "Which roles see which pages, workspace tabs and actions. Read by the backend (services/visibilityService.js) and the frontend (src/lib/visibility.ts).",
    "ceiling: the roles the server could ever allow. The Role visibility page can switch a role off or back on, but never above its ceiling.",
    "default: what applies until a boss changes it. A new resource needs no database row.",
    "locked: roles that always see it and cannot be switched off (keeps a boss from locking themselves out).",
    "enforced: the backend refuses the matching API calls too (requireVisible), not just the screen. Without it, hiding is cosmetic.",
    "A player can never be given anything here: every resource manages something, and the service refuses a ceiling containing player."
  ],
  "roles": ["boss", "super_user", "tournament_host", "player"],
  "roleLabels": {
    "boss": "Boss",
    "super_user": "Super user",
    "tournament_host": "Tournament host",
    "player": "Player"
  },
  "groups": [
    { "id": "admin", "label": "Admin pages" },
    { "id": "workspace", "label": "Tournament workspace tabs" },
    { "id": "actions", "label": "Buttons & actions" }
  ],
